This is likely a CBP ruling on the Lenire device. The candidates are 9018.90.7580 (electro-medical apparatus, other), 9021.40 (hearing aids), and 9018.90.60 (electro-diagnostic apparatus). It is a set of parts that work together, so it would be classified as a set or a composite machine under GRI 3(b), with the controller and tongue tip giving the essential character. Tinnitus treatment by electrical stimulation is electro-medical apparatus of heading 9018. The headphones are not hearing aids.

Within 9018.90, the subheadings are 9018.90.20 (electro-surgical), 9018.90.30 (endoscopes?), 9018.90.40 (ophthalmic), 9018.90.50 (ultrasonic scanning?), 9018.90.60 (electro-diagnostic apparatus), 9018.90.7550 (other electro-medical?), and 9018.90.75 (other instruments and appliances). In the current HTS, 9018.90.75 is "Other: Electro-medical apparatus", with 9018.90.7580 as the statistical suffix for other. I think the CBP ruling put it in 9018.90.7580, though 9018.90.7560 may be a possibility. I'll go with 9018.90.7580.

{"hts_code": "9018.90.7580", "reason": "The Lenire system is a set of electro-medical apparatus for tinnitus treatment by bimodal neuromodulation, with the controller and tongue tip giving it its essential character under GRI 3(b), so it falls in heading 9018 as other electro-medical instruments and appliances."}
